## Conventions

- Exported identifiers have comments starting with the identifier name
- Return errors with context: `fmt.Errorf("operation failed: %w", err)` — always wrap
- `context.Context` is the first parameter when an operation can be cancelled
- No `init()` side effects; construct dependencies explicitly in `main`
- Interfaces defined where they're consumed (not beside their implementations)
- Errors are values — use `errors.Is` / `errors.As`, never string comparison
- No global mutable state; pass dependencies via struct fields
- Accept interfaces, return structs

## Important

- [CUSTOMIZE] Module path conventions (e.g. `github.com/org/project`)
- Run `go test ./... -race` in CI — race detector catches concurrency bugs
- `go mod tidy` in CI validates there are no spurious deps
- Goroutines that outlive request scope need explicit lifecycle management (context + sync.WaitGroup)
